roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.03745896123578879,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":45.8,"_gate_pool_share":-0.16834248018843034,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.05012791778636361,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":50.1,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.08318104586671926,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.00980463585176124,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":40.2,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.024810209334681477,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":81.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.012758116211023813,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":78.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.18115,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.111,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":11.1,"pf":[],"description_full":"RH, together with its subsidiaries, operates as a retailer and lifestyle brand in the home furnishings market in the United States, Canada, the United Kingdom, Germany, Belgium, and Spain. The company operates in three segments: RH Segment, Waterworks, and Real Estate. It offers merchandise in various categories, including furniture, lighting, textiles, bath ware, d\u00e9cor, and outdoor and garden furnishings, as well as baby, child, and teen furnishings. The company also operates galleries, interior design studios, outlets, guesthouses, and showrooms. It sells its products through hospitality, websites, sourcebooks, and trade and contract channels, as well as retail locations and outlets. The company was formerly known as Restoration Hardware Holdings, Inc. and changed its name to RH in January 2017. RH was founded in 1980 and is headquartered in Corte Madera, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Gary G. Friedman | Chairman & CEO | Age 67 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $528K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 8%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $39K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["RH is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $2.5B market cap on $3.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 25% against a 12% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 39%.","The business throws off $252M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.62\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 18% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (58.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 38% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.38050626069723426},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $21.8M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-21802828.89},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 46% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"RH (NYSE:RH) Stock Falls 6.1% \u2013 Here\u2019s What Happened","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/rh-nyserh-stock-falls-6-1-heres-what-happened.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793725579.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(RH) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/23/RH_Movement_as_an_Input_in_Quant_Signal_Sets_110326074801_179